            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Electricity, hard coal, at power plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="a7a7aa24-604f-3bc6-a698-545bafdf915d">electricity by fuel</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="1e16a4cb-ccc6-35f7-b15f-24774dfc57ec">coal</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The module describes the electricity production of an average plant for the country. The plant is used for middle load with 4000 hours of operation at full capacity per year. The plant is assumed to operate 150000 hours during its lifetime. For the assessment of main characteristics (LHV, sulphur and ash content of coal, efficiency of the plant) and criteria emissions (SOx, NOx, particles, and CO2) a bottom-up approach has been used. It consists on the collection of information about single plants. Base data on all major UCTE power plants in 1993 have been integrated, to the extent possible, with updated information for year 2000. The size distribution of particles has been derived from German data. Halogene emissions have been estimated on the basis of the content of the species in the country-specific coal input mix, assuming average retention rates. For CO and VOC-emissions average values for UCTE are included. Two average values for N2O emissions from UCTE plants are considered for the two cases with or without DeNOx;
UUID: a7de413f-be74-32c4-85a0-9a15f6b2f896</common:generalComment>
